      "title": "yosoi::locators::Finding::try_new",
      "kind": "function",
      "signature": "pub fn try_new(document_id: yosoi::DocumentId, output_id: yosoi::locators::OutputId, order: u64, coordinate: yosoi::locators::NativeCoordinate, value: yosoi::locators::ProjectedValue, completeness: yosoi::locators::Completeness, parent_region: Option<yosoi::locators::RegionLineage>) -> Result<Self, FindingError>",
      "docs": "Creates an owned finding after checking projected node-reference identity.\n\n`document_id`, `output_id`, and `order` label the finding; `coordinate`\nlocates its evidence, and `parent_region` records optional repeated-region\nlineage. `completeness` is the supplied evidence claim, not independently\nverified by this constructor. For node projections, returns\n[`FindingError`] if the projected document or coordinate disagrees.\nOther projected values are accepted without document I/O.",
